{
  "id": "subarray-product-less-than-k",
  "questionId": "subarray-product-less-than-k",
  "slug": "subarray-product-less-than-k",
  "title": "Subarray Product Less Than K",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "variable-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "since all numbers are positive, if a window's product is already under k, what do you know about every subarray ending at the same right edge but starting further right?",
    "grow the window to the right, multiplying into a running product",
    "if the product ever reaches k or more, shrink from the left (dividing out), until the product is under k again",
    "here's the key trick: once a window [left, right] is valid, every subarray ending at 'right' and starting anywhere from 'left' to 'right' is also valid - that's (right - left + 1) new subarrays to add to your count, not just 1"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "only counting the window itself as one valid subarray, instead of counting all sub-windows ending at the current right edge",
    "not handling k <= 1 as an immediate zero, since a product can never be negative or less than 1 with positive integers other than through an empty product",
    "using division to shrink the window in a language/context where the product could overflow before the check happens"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of positive integers and an integer `k`.\n\n**Count how many contiguous subarrays have a product strictly less than k.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 3 * 10^4",
      "1 <= nums[i] <= 1000",
      "0 <= k <= 10^6"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "k = 0 or k = 1 (no subarray can have a product that small, since all elements are positive integers)",
      "k larger than the product of the whole array (every subarray counts)",
      "a single element array"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
